# Changeset Editor Frontend - Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and update values as needed

# API Base URL
# Default: /api (relative path, uses Vite proxy)
# For production or different backend: http://localhost:8002/api
VITE_API_BASE=/api

# Development Server Port
# Default: 3000 (configured in vite.config.ts)
# Can be overridden with --port flag: npm run dev -- --port 3001

# Notes:
# - All Vite environment variables must be prefixed with VITE_
# - Variables are available in code via import.meta.env.VITE_API_BASE
# - The .env file should be added to .gitignore (already configured)
# - In development, Vite proxy forwards /api requests to http://127.0.0.1:8001
# - For production builds, set VITE_API_BASE to your production API URL
